    {
      "id": "claim_6713c27f22db40249f2aa343f6915341",
      "statement": "components/trusted-actions/openapi/ is the hand-maintained source of truth for the HTTP contract, split into openapi.yaml (entrypoint: metadata, servers, paths map, security declarations), components/ (reusable schemas and the ocm_jwt security scheme definition), and paths/ (one file per route, $ref'd from openapi.yaml); oapi-codegen (configured via oapi-codegen.yaml) generates internal/openapi/api.go — a chi-compatible server interface plus request/response models — from this spec, while internal/rta is entirely hand-written Go client/CLI code that imports the generated internal/openapi types but is not itself generated.",
